#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308688 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95223ee8-46d8-58c2-9e3b-017adb2789e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution of an Inhomogeneous System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d4bfced-4c23-541f-b242-4c2ea02d35eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306347} {:answer/id #uuid "72e16707-4ff3-5dfd-9eed-366cbfa6fe18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72e16707-4ff3-5dfd-9eed-366cbfa6fe18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479531} :answer-field/id #uuid "52d98b8a-0ce9-5cfa-a498-ed17c16b2e6d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307772} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1c22720-1aa8-597e-9b76-8432cec4de4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307375} {:answer/id #uuid "27dc7621-01eb-5ac6-8247-fe730465d634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27dc7621-01eb-5ac6-8247-fe730465d634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479418} :answer-field/id #uuid "cba95706-4eaf-526e-986f-73babc57c464" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "001f1d7b-e465-5a31-aa71-fce5efbdd939" :question/math-academy-id "q-334824" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$(t-s){e}^{3t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{3s}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(t-s){e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}(t-s){e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308696 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95223ee8-46d8-58c2-9e3b-017adb2789e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution of an Inhomogeneous System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b12c1e03-c805-5e36-aea2-b6d121e73478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(4(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306815} {:answer/id #uuid "74474233-2fa8-51ba-9cb4-da5296695f41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(4(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74474233-2fa8-51ba-9cb4-da5296695f41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(4(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479536} :answer-field/id #uuid "13f5abdf-75a7-5b21-afa3-653d497c5d41" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307584} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab25cf3f-5e10-5e03-b9ec-f148d948ee64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306768} {:answer/id #uuid "677ff288-ab7f-56c0-a677-5f7330959d63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "677ff288-ab7f-56c0-a677-5f7330959d63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479513} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f9d3c90-4891-5e53-85e9-0abe74fcc6f2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7c3b7f24-1005-522b-87d6-a7afb67ecc23" :question/math-academy-id "q-334858" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479848 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95223ee8-46d8-58c2-9e3b-017adb2789e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution of an Inhomogeneous System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1469716d-c345-5ffe-8890-e1981e80d56a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479390} {:answer/id #uuid "3a5c4e43-e417-5c07-a2c3-eb9628d96e3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)-3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479445} {:answer/id #uuid "740b8e1d-0233-597c-ac41-6431abd888f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479535} {:answer/id #uuid "deba3bee-d355-5039-ab99-fbef85ee9df4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "740b8e1d-0233-597c-ac41-6431abd888f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479535} :answer-field/id #uuid "4952d3ec-dd70-5ca3-b11d-7bddbd2cbfa1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479768} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13688bbb-8a94-53d1-b777-8b7a97c5b5a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479387} {:answer/id #uuid "76d12e8f-d604-5766-8275-33330f073e0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479538} {:answer/id #uuid "c13c88e1-4c54-5e6c-a695-0823d83ecac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t+s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479648} {:answer/id #uuid "e7edf428-062b-5000-bf1d-efff0567c499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t+s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479702}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76d12e8f-d604-5766-8275-33330f073e0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479538} :answer-field/id #uuid "d776bb26-ce4b-5844-8f89-c1e2c8830a03" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "462afb47-f28d-50fb-a384-b84e85e58f07" :question/math-academy-id "q-334920" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"160px\">$\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td><td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"160px\">${e}^{4s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{4s}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{4s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{4s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308724 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eca32dd-1563-55c6-b594-08588efd601b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inhomogeneous System Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8e79b01-2389-5a91-bd1b-47d545c124e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307021} {:answer/id #uuid "06fe7ba9-e60a-5a45-b758-fa0196ee521e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06fe7ba9-e60a-5a45-b758-fa0196ee521e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479370} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c1add94-bde4-538a-ae6f-d06b8a3019c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "19468931-2ce6-5bd0-af7b-5212e5297c87" :question/math-academy-id "q-335085" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=5x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=5y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x(0) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5t}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5t}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5t}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eca32dd-1563-55c6-b594-08588efd601b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inhomogeneous System Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "445c6a63-f339-5ff2-afa4-e26785fbf1f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396567} {:answer/id #uuid "96de3917-2210-5111-9750-f9437e72cfa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396568} {:answer/id #uuid "875915a9-2dd7-5bfd-a876-9d427aa8a55b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396569} {:answer/id #uuid "ba2a0cc9-e777-59ad-9b3f-6332bbbb90e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96de3917-2210-5111-9750-f9437e72cfa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396568} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e1c7d9a-e955-5ffd-bbe8-c5635e09bdc8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2b8ad61-9b47-5971-9495-e31b2ea4691b" :question/math-academy-id "q-335175" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=2x(t)+2,\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
